      "philpapers_id": "STERMA",
      "snippet": "He is a substance monist and a pluralist about what kinds of things exist. Nevertheless, Spinoza has often been read as a materialist, and one prominent strand of this materialist reading may be traced back to the Russian Marxist Georgi Plekhanov, who, beginning in the 1890s, engaged in a series of polemics in which he defended a comprehensive materialist reading of Spinoza\u2014one that would cover both ontological and dialectical materialism, or \u201cold\u201d and \u201cnew\u201d materialism\u2014that would cement Spinoza\u2019s status as the great progenitor of political radicalism.",
